From 1b9eebafb963134687f7c7bf7319dc0251f92316 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 12:06:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] test(r57): the decider answers - past the mat-vec boundary a
 verify column is ~46x cheaper

Head shape 248320x5120 (the served lm_head, q4_K), 3 rounds, same-config band 0.8%
median / 1.1% max - the cleanest of the three. Read off the INHERITED arm alone, so
mat-vec below 9 and GEMM above it with no switch involved and none of the forced arm's
penalty band in the comparison:

  n=1..8   8975 9273 9779 11655 13012 13593 14570 15533 us   marg(4..8) = 969 us/col
  n=9..16  19175 ... 19324 us (flat)                          marg(9..16) = 21 us/col

One extra verify column costs 969 us inside the mat-vec regime and 21 us past it, with a
one-time 3642 us step at n=8->9. Forced GEMM at n<=8 is 2.4x worse than mat-vec, so there
is no crossing below 9 on any of the three shapes or any of the four types.

Per the pre-registered rule that is outcome two: the lever is n-max in the DFlash2 driver,
not the admit switch. And marg(4..8) is a band average, not a rate - its per-column steps
are +298/+506/+1876/+1357/+581/+977/+963, where the +1876 is the width-4 knee section 2
measures at 16.4% on this same shape.

The head also makes the GEMM n=5..8 penalty band general rather than an ffn artifact
(21.2k / 24.1k / 19.1k us at a 0.8% band on a shape 16x larger), so it gets its registry
row. Correctness re-taken at the final binary: 71/71 both arms, rc 0, and the admit-width
line appears in the =0 receipt and not in the default one, which is the arm's own proof.

Origin: fork-authored (ArifiLabs lane-248 R57 q4_K cheaper dot, Opus 5 MEDIUM kernel-maker)
Measured-effect: op-level perf-mode only (rows in receipts); no default moves, no shipped path touched; served t/s UNMEASURED by the maker - HQ pairs quiet
Lane: lane-248
Cherry-picked-from: b8051b0d6 (SOURCE PATHS ONLY, ArifiLabs lane-254 R66 integration)
Recut-onto: 668641bc0 (ArifiLabs lane-254 R66c, from fe361f814)
