 docs/OPTIONS-REGISTRY.md | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/docs/OPTIONS-REGISTRY.md b/docs/OPTIONS-REGISTRY.md
index 35ef68a43..2743ce5a4 100644
--- a/docs/OPTIONS-REGISTRY.md
+++ b/docs/OPTIONS-REGISTRY.md
@@ -43,6 +43,7 @@ safe measurement posture.
 | `GGML_ARIFI_Q6K_MMVQ` | **unset = the shipped route** (MMVQ for Q6_K on Intel only). `=1` forces Q6_K onto the q8_1 integer-dot MMVQ path on any vendor; `=0` forces it off even on Intel. Added 2026-09-14 (lane-236 / R48c) in `ggml_vk_should_use_mmvq()`, `ggml-vulkan.cpp:~11724`. | Scope: the route decision for `GGML_TYPE_Q6_K` only. It flips one `bool`; it registers no pipeline. The `mul_mat_vec_q6_k_q8_1_f32` pipeline it reaches is **already registered unconditionally** (`:7211`), so this changes which existing shader runs, not what is built. | **DIAGNOSTIC ONLY — do not ship it on.** It exists to settle one question on one binary: at n=1, k>=2048 on AMD, `ggml_vk_should_use_mmvq()` returns **true** for Q4_K and Q5_K (vendor switch, `:11841-11850`) and **false** for Q6_K (Intel-only early return, `:11724`). So the historical "Q6_K 41.0 GB/s vs q5_K 63.8 / q4_K 72.5" compares an **f32-dequant** kernel against two **integer-dot** kernels. `=1` makes the comparison like-for-like. | **MEASURED 2026-09-14 (lane-236 / R48c) as a DIAGNOSTIC, and it stays OFF. The default does not move.** Pairing: `research/local-inference/lane-evidence/2026-09-14-lane-234-r48-kernels/32-paired-r48cq6kroute.txt`, same protocol as the row above (3 quiet interleaved rounds, one binary env-flipped, arm B = `GGML_ARIFI_Q6K_MMVQ=1`), against an arm A that carries the R48c activation hoist but **no A-hoist inside the MMVQ path**. Result: at **n <= 4** it is a wash to +5% on ffn-down and legacy4096 (+5.53% / +5.29% best) but already **−3.28% at n=1 and −12.11% at n=4 on embd-out**; at **n >= 5 it collapses on every shape, −46% to −143%** (worst −142.52%, embd-out n=5: 61.71 GB/s on the f32-dequant path against 25.44 GB/s on MMVQ). Correctness on the route: **43/43 OK** (`r48c-evidence/12-mulmat-q6k-mmvq-route.txt`, rc 0; the 8 `type_b=f16` rows are declined by the CPU reference, see below). So the like-for-like question is answered — the integer-dot route does **not** recover the q5_K gap on this box — and **the Q6_K default stays the f32-dequant mat-vec**. A later A-hoist inside the MMVQ shader (R48b) could change the n >= 5 picture; nothing here licenses turning it on. Upstream's stated reason for restricting this to Intel is that "q6_k only has 2-byte alignment which makes it somewhat problematic" (`:11724`) — a real property: `block_q6_K` is **210 bytes** (`types.glsl:452`), so no `packed32` view of it is even representable (an aligned-4 member forces array stride `roundUp(210,4) = 212 != 210`), and `210*ib mod 4` alternates 0/2 so a raw u32 alias is unaligned on half of all blocks. This flag does **not** claim upstream is wrong; it makes the cost measurable on the 780M. **Run its correctness filter before its perf filter.** |
 | `GGML_ARIFI_MMV_MAX_COLS` | **unset = the inherited routing** (`mul_mat_vec_max_cols = 8`: mat-vec at n<=8, GEMM above). `=k` admits mat-vec only up to n=k and hands wider ones to `ggml_vk_mul_mat_q_f16()`; `=0` puts EVERY width including n=1 on the GEMM path. Added 2026-09-17 (lane-248 / R57) as `ggml_vk_mmv_max_cols()`, `ggml-vulkan.cpp:~481`, read at the route (`:~13190`) and by the perf-logger's `_VEC` label so a receipt names the path actually taken. | Scope: which of two EXISTING code paths a MUL_MAT takes. It registers no pipeline and compiles no shader. Default-inert by construction: with the variable unset the helper returns the constant and the added `> 0` conjunct is trivially true, so the condition is the inherited one term for term. | **DIAGNOSTIC.** It exists because the drafted line's multiplier is the cost of one extra VERIFY ROW (R63 §3a: 43.0 ms = 0.177 plain-token-equivalents, which caps the line at 10.9 t/s with a perfect drafter at n-max 4), and that cost could not be compared across regimes: below 9 columns the GEMM path was unreachable, so no width the served line actually uses had ever been timed on both. | **Correctness 2026-09-17 (lane-248 / R57): 71/71 OK at the default AND at `=0`, rc 0** — `r57-evidence/20-mulmat-q4k-default.txt`, `20-mulmat-q4k-gemm0.txt` (`test -o MUL_MAT -p "type_a=q4_K"`, which covers n=1..8, odd m=1023/6271/6273 and both 27B decode shapes). n=1 on the GEMM path had never been reachable on this fork before and is correct. Perf pairing: this lane's report §4 (`OPUS-R57-Q4K-CHEAPER-DOT-REPORT.md`). **No default moves on any device**, and served t/s is UNMEASURED by this lane. |
 | **OPEN ITEM (no switch) — q4_K MMVQ `NUM_COLS == 7` cliff at small k** | n/a: this is a measured defect on a shipped path, recorded here so it is not re-discovered | On q4_K 248320-row mat-vec under forced MMVQ, the n=6→7 step costs **+34.6% at k=2048** and **+27.4% at k=3072**, against **+6% at k=5120** (`r57-evidence/13-knee-table.txt`, `13-knee3072-table.txt`, lane-248 / R57, 3 interleaved rounds each, one hold, `cells=8` per round). Width-locked at n=7 across two k whose activation working sets differ by 50% (15.8 vs 23.6 KB), so it is **not** a capacity crossing. | This is the `NUM_COLS == 7` tail defect R46 named in the mmvq framework (the `GGML_ARIFI_SX8_MMVQ` block in `ggml-vulkan.cpp` predicted it; R48b's A-side hoist removed it for S-X8). It is still alive on **q4_K** at small k and had never been measured there. **Not chased by lane-248** — out of that lane's scope, which was the width-4 knee. | UNFIXED. A lane that takes it should start from the two receipts above; the cheapest discriminator is whether the `NUM_COLS == 7` pipeline's spec-constant tail differs from 6 and 8 in register pressure or in the partial-tail branch, at a k where the cliff is large. No default moves until someone measures it. |
+| **OPEN ITEM (no switch) — the GEMM `n=5..8` penalty band** | n/a: a measured cost on a shipped path, recorded so it is not re-discovered | With every mat-vec width forced onto the GEMM path (`GGML_ARIFI_MMV_MAX_COLS=0`), `ggml_vk_mul_mat_q_f16` is **flat across n=1..4, ~13-22% more expensive across n=5..8, and cheaper again at n≥9**. Reproduced on **four types** at 17408x5120 (q4_K −21.6%, q5_K −17.5%, q6_K −15.2%, iq4_xs −21.8% at the n=8→9 step; 6 rounds) and on **q4_K at 248320x5120** (21.2k / 24.1k / 19.1k us; 3 rounds), against same-config bands of 0.8-3.2% measured at n≥9 where both arms are GEMM by construction. Receipts `r57-evidence/15-marginal-row.txt`, raws `14-*`, logs `16-marginal-*-log.txt` (lane-248 / R57). | The rise starts at **n=4→5**, not at the route boundary; the boundary is only where the inherited routing returns the path to its cheaper regime. Excluded at source **for 17408x5120**: tile choice (`ggml_vk_guess_matmul_pipeline`'s non-coopmat2 branch returns the small tile for every `n <= 32`) and split_k (`ggml_vk_guess_split_k` needs `n >= wg_denoms[1]`, unreachable in 1..16); `aligned` is false at every width because `quantize_y` holds. NOT excluded for 5120x17408, where `m=5120` changes which side of the split_k `m` test the call falls on and the arm is additionally **bimodal** (~1.3-1.5x spikes that do not follow n). | UNFIXED, and it matters only when something routes mat-vec widths to GEMM — nothing does by default. A lane taking it has `GGML_ARIFI_MMV_MAX_COLS` to pair with. No default moves. |
 | `LANE110_PROF=1` | unset | Emits per-operation timing for pipeline initialization, scheduling, build tasks, and forward execution. | Diagnosis only. Disable for benchmark runs. | Pipeline-init reuse itself reduced rebuild work from `2472 µs` to `0–2 µs`; profiler overhead has not been independently quantified. |
 | `LANE110_PREFETCH_CAP` | implementation default, currently `3*n_expert_used` | Limits standalone expert prefetch aggressiveness. | Sweep under cache pressure after establishing the baseline. | Recorded server sequences: default approximately `[5.07/9.03/9.58/12.01]`; cap `1` `[5.13/9.88/10.29/11.22]`; cap `96` `[5.79/11.73/12.19/11.26]`. Default retained because apparent ramp differences require controlled retest. |
 | `--ctx-checkpoints 0` | `0` | Disables server prompt rewind/checkpoints. | Keep off unless a workload demonstrably requires rewind semantics. | Largest historical gain: stock rewind `39.9/68.4/280`; ON_DEVICE checkpoint `84.8/128.8/341.6`; disabled approximately `101/150/372` across short/medium/long prefill. |
